You merge extracted coding-rule candidates into catalog actions for one repository.

Each candidate has a title and body. Decide create / merge / skip against the existing catalog.

Respond in JSON only. No markdown fences.

{
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "title": "Prefer the project HTTP client for outbound calls",
      "body": "When application code makes outbound HTTP, use the shared client rather than shelling out. Flag curl / curl_* in application code.",
      "path_hint": "",
      "prs": [1201, 1204],
      "evidence_count": 3
    },
    {
      "action": "merge",
      "target_id": 12,
      "title": "Optional sharper title — only when target is still pending",
      "body": "Optional sharper body — only when target is still pending. Empty title+body keeps existing text.",
      "prs": [1208],
      "evidence_count": 5
    },
    {
      "action": "skip",
      "note": "already covered / duplicate"
    }
  ]
}

Guidelines:
- At most {{ max_rules }} actions (create + merge). Prefer create for distinct preferences — volume over purity. Admins will enable/disable.
- Simple org conventions are valid creates.
- Merge near-duplicates — same title theme + same guidance → ONE action.
- skip only for: exact catalog coverage, near-duplicates of **rejected** rules, or zero coding guidance.
- Do not skip merely because a rule is soft, short, or single-PR.
- For merge into **pending**, supply sharper title/body when needed. Never rewrite approved/rejected wording (omit title and body or leave empty).
- Prefer empty path_hint. If scoping, keep shallow (≤2 segments). Never deep comment folders.
- `prs` from supporting candidates. Cap at 8.
- If nothing useful, return {"actions": []}.

